course: dictionary
lesson: 6203
title: One word, many meanings: miss
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word miss has several meanings, and the words around it show you which one to use. «I missed the ball» means I did not hit or catch it. «I missed the bus» means I was too late for it.
explain: Miss can also mean to feel sad because someone is not with you. «Missing a brother who has left home is natural; calls, letters and talking help.» The clues are calls, letters and talking, so missing here means feeling sad that he is away.
explain: Miss can be a noun too: a miss is a failed try. A capital M, as in Miss, is a title for a girl or unmarried woman. Ask yourself: is there a verb, a noun, or a capital letter? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Miss as a verb can mean to fail to hit, catch or reach something.
fact: Missed the bus or train means you were too late for it.
fact: Missing someone means feeling sad because they are not with you.
fact: Miss with a capital letter is a title, and many UK and Irish children call a female teacher «Miss!».
fact: In maths, a missing number puzzle asks you to find the number that fits: 5 + ? = 12, so the missing number is 12 − 5 = 7.
exercise: «I missed the ball.» What does missed mean here? | Threw it to a friend | * Failed to hit or catch it | Caught it easily | Kicked it very hard
exercise: «Missing a brother who has left home is natural.» What does missing mean here? | Finding him in a game | Looking at the house | * Feeling sad because he is not with you | Hiding from him
exercise: In maths, 5 + ? = 12. What is the missing number? | 17 | 6 | 8 | * 7
test: Lily says, «Miss, can I go to the toilet?» Who is Miss? | * Her female teacher | A bus driver | A famous singer | Her big sister
test: «She missed the train because she woke up late.» What does missed mean? | * Was too late for it | Found it again | Ran faster than the train | Did not hit it
exam: Which sentence uses miss to mean feel sad because someone is gone? | «I missed the goal.» | * «I miss my grandad since he moved away.» | «Miss Patel said well done.» | «I missed the bus this morning.»
